  "openQuestions": [
    "Base tabs (press, happenings, blog) are in-page anchors to the category headings below. Nothing moves is-active as the reader scrolls, so the first tab stays active. Accept static, add a small scroll-spy module, or are happenings and blog tabs meant to be CMS filters (Finsweet) for Q029?",
    "The vision review calls the pill nav 'floating'. Should the base pill nav stay sticky while the reader scrolls the cards below? The plan keeps it static.",
    "Custom attributes are fixed in the component, so base instances also carry data-scroll-enlarge-snap. With an empty panels slot the module returns early but logs a console warning on press, happenings and blog. Accept, or make scrollEnlargeSnap skip silently when a root has no items (one-line change in src/utils/scrollEnlargeSnap.ts)?",
    "Q021 home 04 to 09 uses the same pinned stage and frame without an intro. K01: promote tab-pills-intro_stage and tab-pills-intro_frame (is-media) to a shared pair (suggested enlarge-snap_stage, enlarge-snap_frame) if P021 plans its own.",
    "Meetings tab labels (terrace, conference center) do not match the Q021 panel titles (lobby terrace, 1 america plaza). Which copy is right?",
    "The Figma file has no mobile or tablet frames for these sections; all non-desktop values are proposals.",
    "At 390 wide a long tab row scrolls sideways inside the pill (the last label is clipped, e.g. 'confe' on meetings) with no visible scroll cue. Accept, add an edge fade, or let the tabs wrap on mobile?"
  ],
  "deviations": [
    "Three brief variants become one modifier, is-media. All three references centre their text (the brief's 'left-aligned' is a vision-review error), so is-centered changes nothing; is-1-image and is-tall both come from the media frame. The meetings frame is the same frame with Figma's #D9D9D9 placeholder where its first panel image will go.",
    "The wellness frame image (asset 6ad67000240d911fb18d77af) is the first Q021 panel's image (it is also used by wellness-collection/03), so tab-pills-intro has no image of its own: the frame holds a panels slot for Q021 venue cards.",
    "The H3-CAPS 'press' and 'dining' labels at the bottom of the base crops belong to the next section (press/03, happenings/03), so the brief's heading-size content note (h3-caps vs morello-80) does not apply. Every instance uses heading-style-h1 + text-style-script.",
    "Heading colour is #000000 in the wellness and meetings references and #29310C in the base references. The plan inherits color-accent (#29310C) everywhere.",
    "Paragraph widths in the references are 588, 636 and 660px; the plan uses one max-width of 37.5rem.",
    "The base and media instances share one Webflow component; 'media' is a Webflow component variant that applies is-media to the component, header, stage, frame and tabs elements.",
    "Q023 build: the `tabs` and `panels` slots are not slots. The props API has no slot type (Q022 finding). The definition holds four fixed tab links with label and url link props, and Show tab 4 (default off) covers the three-tab and four-tab instances. The panels slot is left for the Designer; the Q021 venue cards cannot be dropped into the frame until it exists.",
    "Q023 build: the `media` Webflow component variant is not built. The is-media look is two plain reference sections on the build page (wellness with 4 tabs, meetings with 3), following the Q017, Q019, Q020 and Q021 precedent; V01 decides the per-instance variant route.",
    "Q023 build: the heading aria-label is bound to the Heading prop, so it carries the same line break as the heading text (\"A room\\nfor every stay\"). The reference sections use a static one-line aria-label.",
    "Q023 build: the definition's first tab carries `is-active` statically, so base instances show the first tab active and scrollEnlargeSnap moves it on media instances."
  ],
  "k01": {
    "reconciledBy": "K01, 2026-10-20",
    "sharedClasses": "docs/figma/build-plans/shared-classes.md",
    "changes": [
      "Class list `tab-pills-intro_heading heading-style-h1 text-style-script` is now `tab-pills-intro_heading text-style-script is-large`.",
      "The `is-media` modifier is kept: the brief's `is-media-center + is-1-image + is-tall` and `is-centered + is-tall` both reduce to the same frame, and every reference is centred (see deviations).",
      "Script heading is `text-style-script is-large`. The live `text-style-eyebrow-caps` has no mobile step, so the tab labels stay 18px on mobile (the plan proposed 16px).",
      "Variables use live CSS names (`--_primitives---colors--*`, `--_typography---font-styles--*`)."
    ]
  },
